# NewUnera — WCAG 2.2 Level AA (product HTML)

**Scope:** All files under [`NewUnera/`](NewUnera/) (`*.html`). [`NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html`](NewUnera/brand-style-guide.html) may include marketing specimens; interactive demos there must still avoid unreadable text/ink combinations.

**Normative baseline:** [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/) **Level AA**. For static HTML UI, prioritize:

| Criterion | Requirement |
|-----|-----|
| **1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum)** | Normal text **≥ 4.5:1**; large text (≥18pt regular or 14pt bold) **≥ 3:1** vs background |
| **1.4.11 Non-text Contrast** | UI components and graphical objects that convey state **≥ 3:1** (borders, icons that communicate meaning, focus rings) |
| **2.4.7 Focus Visible** | Every interactive control has a visible focus indicator (see [`new-brand-output.mdc`](new-brand-output.mdc) — `outline` with `--brand-deep-blue` on light surfaces, `--brand-yellow` on dark nav) |
| **2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum)** | **24×24 CSS px** minimum (WCAG 2.2); product bar remains **≥ 44–46px** for primary actions per workspace design rules |

Also align with existing project requirements: **skip link** (`href="#main-content"`), **`prefers-reduced-motion`**, **`lang`** on `<html>`, meaningful **`alt`** / decorative images, **`aria-*`** where components need it, logical **heading order**, **labels** on inputs.

## Brand-specific contrast rules (UNERA V2)

### Warm / pale surfaces (`--gradient-warm`)

On product pages, `--gradient-warm` is a **pale tint** (`color-mix` of `--brand-yellow` and white). **Do not** use **`--brand-white`**, **`white`**, or **`--brand-yellow`** as **text or icon ink** on that background — contrast fails **1.4.3**.

**Correct pattern:** `color: var(--brand-deep-blue)` (and optional `border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-deep-blue) 18%, transparent)` for pill edges). Matches [`.cursor/rules/newunera-color-system.mdc`](newunera-color-system.mdc) §7.6 (warm badge / lightning accent copy).

### `--neutral-500` and text

In V2 `:root`, **`--neutral-500`** maps to **`#90c2b8`** (`--brand-light-blue` family). **Do not use it for text** (body, labels, captions, placeholders, meta lines) on white or light `--surface-*` cards — it **fails 1.4.3** on typical backgrounds.

**Use instead:** **`var(--text-secondary)`** (`#3d6b78`) or **`var(--neutral-600)`** where the token stack matches (often equivalent). **Reserved uses for `--neutral-500`:** non-text pairings only when contrast is verified (e.g. some disabled **background** recipes — still verify **1.4.3** for any visible **text** on that control).

### Decorative vs informative icons

Per [`.cursor/rules/newunera-icons.mdc`](newunera-icons.mdc): inline SVGs use **`fill="currentColor"`**. Purely decorative glyphs: **`aria-hidden="true"`**. Do not use emoji for UI affordances where Material inline SVG is specified.

## Checklist before merging NewUnera UI changes

- [ ] New or updated **badges / pills / captions**: contrast spot-check (warm tint → deep-blue ink; no light-blue-on-white small text).
- [ ] New **buttons / links / cards**: **focus-visible** present; no `outline: none` without a visible replacement.
- [ ] **Forms:** associated labels (visible or `aria-label`); error text readable (e.g. `--error` on sufficient surface).
- [ ] **Images:** meaningful `alt`; decorative `alt=""`.
- [ ] **Keyboard:** tab through the changed flow; focus order makes sense.
- [ ] **Motion:** respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations/transitions.

## Verification workflow (recommended)

1. Open the page locally and run **axe DevTools** or **Lighthouse** (Accessibility) on the changed screen.
2. Manually tab through primary and secondary actions.
3. For contentious pairs, use a contrast checker (e.g. WebAIM) on computed foreground/background.

**Note:** Claiming “100% WCAG 2.2 AA” for an entire static site requires a full audit; use the checklist + tooling above for each change set.

